)ATTR DEFAULT(@}_)
 @ TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(WHITE)
 } TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(GREEN)
 { TYPE(TEXT)   INTENS(LOW)  COLOR(TURQ)
 _ TYPE(INPUT)  INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(RED)    CAPS(ON) JUST(LEFT)
 ! TYPE(OUTPUT) INTENS(HIGH) COLOR(YELLOW) CAPS(OFF) JUST(LEFT)
)BODY
@HELP: Using Help and the Tutorial              !ISFHMSG                      }
@COMMAND INPUT ===>_ISFHCMD                                                  }
}
}  The help describes every SDSF panel: its command, its action characters,
}  its fields and the commands you can give on it. The tutorial, started
}  with the TUTOR command, is a short course through SDSF.
}
}  On a help or tutorial panel:
{    Enter            }shows the next panel of the topic
{    a number         }shows the topic of that number, where topics are listed
{    Up key, PF7      }goes up to the panel that lists this topic
{    Left key, PF10   }goes back to the panel shown before
{    T                }shows the table of contents of the help
{    I                }shows the index
{    Help key, PF1    }shows this panel
{    End key, PF3     }leaves the help, back to the SDSF panel
}
}  The keys named are those of the ISPF defaults. SDSF goes by the command
}  a key carries (UP, LEFT, HELP, END); you can also type the command.
}  SDSF commands such as ST are not taken on help panels.
}
}  Enter: contents   T: contents   I: index   PF3: back to SDSF
)PROC
  &ISFHPFK = .PFKEY
  &ZCONT = ISFHTOC
  &ZUP = ISFHTOC
)END
